      en: 'Inani Beach lies south of Cox’s Bazar town in Ukhiya upazila, reached along the Marine Drive with hills on one side and the sea on the other — the journey is half the pleasure. Being away from the main town, it feels far calmer than the central beach points.\n\nAt low tide a field of dark rocks appears along the shore, often called coral rocks by visitors. Tiny rock pools between them shelter snails, crabs and other small sea creatures, and the rocks break the surf so the water is gentler here.\n\nIn winter at low tide the rocks are most exposed and the afternoon light makes them glow. At high tide they disappear under the water and Inani looks like an ordinary sandy beach, so timing your visit with the tide makes a big difference.',
